  "brief": [
    "The NIFTY 50 rose 0.51% to 23,053.10 and the Sensex 0.42% to 74,459.53 on Friday, led by IT (up 2.32%) and pharma; the Nifty Midcap 100 fell 0.93% and decliners outnumbered advancers on NSE.",
    "Foreign institutions bought a net ₹3,599 crore and domestic institutions sold ₹818 crore; over October, foreign institutions sold ₹45,162 crore (all provisional). The rupee gained 33 paise to a provisional 94.93 per dollar.",
    "October GST collections rose 22.9% to ₹2.31 lakh crore. Overseas, the Nasdaq fell 2.86% on Friday, and Brent's January contract settled at $113.43 a barrel, up $2.63, after a tanker attack in the Strait of Hormuz."
